turns out the man most famous for  playing the wizarding world's nastiest  teacher was also a dedicated friend a  mentor and an enormous amount of fun to  be around who'd have guessed it Alan  Rickman might be gone but he left us a  lot to think about and a lot to take his  inspiration in January 2016 Rickman died  of pancreatic cancer at 69 he was no  spring chicken but he wasn't  particularly old either fans around the  world mourned the untimely nature of his  passing and it's seeming suddenness had  anyone known he was sick how long had he  been suffering and how severely had it  been publicized how could one beloved  man's passing in an age of such  unprecedented interconnectivity so  shocked the entire world simply put it  was a secret the first new thing the  world learned about Alan Rickman upon  his death was that he had been battling  pancreatic cancer for a few months prior  after being diagnosed in August  following a small stroke pancreatic  cancer sometimes called a silent cancer  takes time to present any symptoms and  is often found after a seemingly  unconnected problem surfaces Rickman  decided to keep the news confined to  close friends and family and soldiered  on with his work as it happened no one  knew what they were going to lose until  he was already gone  the Rickman portrayed many noteworthy  characters Severus Snape Harry Potter's  grouchy potions professor might be the  most memorable of all Snape is  vindictive Moody and even in his moments  of bravery deeply and unrelentingly  cynical it's a fine edge to dance upon  but Rickman made it look easy  for eight films he portrayed Snape with  caustic aplomb and that performance has  become nothing less than iconic that is  the second time you've spoken out of  turn Miss Granger are you incapable of  restraining yourself or do you take  pride in being an insufferable  know-it-all by all accounts it was also  the role that had least to do with his  actual personality when remembering the  actor posthumously colleagues and  friends have repeatedly touched upon his  unrelenting kindness and generosity of  spirit in a tribute for Entertainment  Weekly Kate Winslet mused if there was  one word I could use to really describe  Al it would be kind he was so kind  whenever L would go out to supper and  anyone else would try and pay he would  somehow have phoned ahead or slipped his  credit card ahead of the meal so no one  even got a look at the check  tales of helping hands thoughtful gifts  and general friendliness seemed to  surround Rickman's legacy he wasn't just  passively kind but actively generous  which is about as far from Snape as you  can get younger fans will never know how  heated the debate over Snape's true  loyalties grew back when the Harry  Potter saga was still a work in progress  Snape's motivations were murky and his  actions ambiguous until the very end  when it was finally revealed that he was  on the side of the angels all along  motivated by his deep and lasting love  for Harry's mother Lily though some had  guessed no one knew the full truth for  sure until the story's very final  chapters no one that is except Alan  Rickman it's since come to light that  author JK Rowling told to recommend the  truth about Snape's motivations years  earlier to help inform his performance  according to Rowling what she told him  boiled down to just one word if you  revisit the Potter films this knowledge  will become more readily apparent in  Rickman's performance although he is  sour unrelentingly harsh and sometimes  even outright cruel he returns over and  over again to the side of light and love  his anger at Harry appears so much more  nuanced than at first glance and his  frustration with the growing darkness  around him more pronounced Snape was  always much more than he seemed and  Rickman made that apparent in everything  from overt declarations of loyalty to  the subtlest most fleeting glances  though Rickman's trademark style and  double bass voice made every role he  took on memorable in its own right  arguably one of his best was Alexander  Dane in 1999's Galaxy Quest also an  actor the character of Dane feels  degraded by his role as dr. Lazarus on  the in universe Star Trek equivalent  Galaxy Quest which requires the use of a  complicated and silly looking skull  prosthetic as well as a horde of alien  catchphrases  by grabthar's hammer  [Music]  water savings Galaxy Quest became an  instant cult hit and is often hailed in  Star Trek fandom as a better Trek movie  than some of the official outings  Rickman's performance in particular of  course is held to be one of the film's  most memorable so it's probably no  surprise to find that a sequel was in  the works which was kept totally under  wraps until Rickman's tragic passing put  an end to the project it's a bittersweet  turn of events that access both the  testament to Rickman's acting and a sad  reminder of what could have been there  are few relationships in the Harry  Potter series more charged and complex  than the one between Harry and Snape  after all Harry Potter and the  half-blood Prince pretty much translates  as Harry Potter and Severus Snape Snape  basically gives his life to protect  Harry yet bullies him relentlessly for  years meanwhile Harry loathes Snape to  the point of obsession yet ends up  naming his son after him the  relationship sits at the heart of the  series and the crux of Harry's journey  it's only appropriate then that Alan  Rickman matters so deeply to Daniel  Radcliffe in a Facebook post made after  Rickman's death Radcliffe hailed him as  one of the greatest actors he would ever  work with he continued he is also one of  the loyalists and most supportive people  I've ever met in the film industry  Radcliffe went on to detail Rickman's  kindness and generosity his mastery of  the craft of acting and his wit adding  one particularly heart-wrenching detail  I'm pretty sure he came and saw  everything I ever did on stage both in  London and New York  Rickman's dedication to performance was  legendary but it was easily surpassed by  his devotion to his fellow performers  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

